  "construction": "Reversing fold of a pair-partition CPM CSS code of arXiv:2609.30069 with J = 3, L = 8, P = 36. Parent qubit q = c*P + t. Parent X row (j,s) meets c*P + ((s - E[j][c]) mod P) for each block c. The involution is pi(c*P + t) = sigma[c]*P + ((-t - B[sigma[c]]) mod P). Folded site i pairs the i-th smallest q with q < pi(q) with pi(q). Each parent X row becomes one generator, X where it meets a representative and Z where it meets a partner. E = [[14, 1, 14, 7, 6, 4, 34, 10], [15, 10, 1, 13, 10, 16, 0, 21], [0, 25, 1, 14, 8, 23, 33, 8]], sigma = [7, 3, 6, 1, 5, 4, 2, 0], B = [27, 6, 16, 6, 3, 3, 16, 27].",
